IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `asa-standards`

-- Accounting Standards Act 2007, ss 2, 4, 5, 7, 8(1), 9(3), 10(2), 11(4), 12 and the Schedule -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_accounting-standards-act-2007.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 8(1)`

#ASSERT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a company`
#ASSERT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a registered co-operative society`
#ASSERT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a registered society`
#ASSERT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a registered charity`
#ASSERT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `an institution of a public character`
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a statutory body`
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT NOT `the Committee's standards may be expressed to apply to` `a sole proprietorship`

§ `ss 9(3), 10(2)`

#ASSERT `the standard has force` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the standard has force` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the standard has force` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the standard has force` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the standard has force` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE

